Quirks reproduced rather than fixed:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mcreate_entries[0m mallocs before validating [38;5;10mcount[0m, so [38;5;10mcount <= 0[0m leaks and returns NULL. In Rust, a negative [38;5;10mcount[0m becomes an enormous [38;5;10mtry_reserve_exact[0m request that fails, giving the same NULL result — which is why [38;5;10mmode[0m 1 and 2 return [38;5;10m-1[0m for negative [38;5;10mparam1[0m in both versions.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mprocess_name[0m checks [38;5;10m*dest == '\0'[0m (empty string), not just [38;5;10mdest == NULL[0m, and ignores [38;5;10mmax_len[0m entirely — the copy stays unbounded.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mfind_entry[0m with a negative count computes [38;5;10mend < entries[0m, so the loop never runs; mirrored with an early [38;5;10mNone[0m.[0m[0m
